-- #1185 CONTROL — the SAME multi-module shape as main.mdk with exactly ONE dimension
-- flipped: the module declaring the unrelated type `Doc` is gone from the graph.
-- `medaka run`/`check` load only what the entry transitively imports, so this entry
-- pulls cutil.mdk alone and never sees doc.mdk sitting beside it in this directory.
-- `total` is the same exhaustive function over `List Int`, still in a non-entry module,
-- and here it draws NO diagnostic. That isolates the unrelated type's presence in the
-- graph as the thing that produces the false positive — not `total`, not the
-- non-entry position, not multi-module checking as such.
import cutil.{total}

main = println (total [1, 2, 3])
